<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  cosmon-scheduler — unified patrol scheduler (cron-triggered, TOML-driven).

  One LaunchAgent that fires `cosmon-scheduler tick` every 60 seconds. The
  binary reads `~/.config/cosmon/patrols.toml`, decides which patrols are
  due, and dispatches each as a detached subprocess. Between ticks nothing
  runs — this honours the cosmon "no daemon in core" invariant
  (ADR-016). See crates/cosmon-scheduler/src/lib.rs for the architecture
  and the governing plan at
  .cosmon/state/fleets/default/molecules/idea-20260417-b52d/plan.md.

  Placeholders below use __HOME__ for the operator's home directory. The
  install script (scripts/install-scheduler.sh) substitutes them at load
  time, so this template stays portable across machines.

  StartInterval = 60 (seconds): the top-level clock of the entire patrol
  layer. Changing this cadence is a design decision (see ADR from
  task-20260417-e162), not a config tweak.

  AbandonProcessGroup = true is LOAD-BEARING, not hygiene. This is a
  one-shot job: `cosmon-scheduler tick` returns in milliseconds. By
  default launchd SIGKILLs the whole process group the instant a job's
  main process exits — so every patrol dispatched in `dispatch =
  "detached"` mode died before producing anything, while the scheduler
  had already logged `FIRE <patrol> (pid=... detached)`. Neither `nohup`
  nor `trap '' HUP` helps: the signal is addressed to the group, not to
  the child. Measured on one 60-second patrol over a 48-hour window:
  7276 fires recorded by the scheduler, 114 starts reached the patrol's
  own log, a handful of runs completed — the ticks that happened to last
  long enough to cover the child's work. The index that patrol feeds sat
  frozen about 18 hours with nothing in any log saying so. Remove this
  key and the whole patrol layer goes back to firing into the void,
  silently.

  If you install a new one-shot LaunchAgent that dispatches detached
  work, it needs this key too. `scripts/check-abandon-process-group.sh`
  enumerates the installed candidates.

  NOT auto-installed. The operator runs:
      scripts/install-scheduler.sh install
      scripts/install-scheduler.sh status
      scripts/install-scheduler.sh uninstall
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.cosmon.scheduler</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__HOME__/.local/bin/cosmon-scheduler</string>
        <string>tick</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>

    <!-- Do not remove: see the AbandonProcessGroup paragraph above. -->
    <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.cosmon/logs/cosmon-scheduler.out</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.cosmon/logs/cosmon-scheduler.err</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>__HOME__</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>__HOME__</string>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:__HOME__/.local/bin:__HOME__/.cargo/bin</string>
        <key>RUST_LOG</key>
        <string>info</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
